.nh
.TH "PB-POLICY-SCHEMA" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-policy-schema - Print the policy file JSON Schema


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb policy schema [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the JSON Schema of the workspace policy file, for editors that check and
complete the file as you type. The schema is built into pb, so this command
works offline and needs no sign-in; it matches the schema the server serves.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for schema


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb policy schema > policy.schema.json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-policy(1)\fP
